  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 239 PM EDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nFor the back half of the work week a front will stall out across the \nsouth, temperatures remain in the upper 80s and lower 90s but rain \ncooled afternoons will give the northern part of the CWA a break \nfrom the heat. Chances of afternoon thunderstorms will continue into \nthe weekend and thanks to Tropical Storm Bertha's influx of moisture \nfrom the gulf some of those storms may be extremely efficient rain \nproducers. The concern for flash flooding will continue through the \nweekend as PW values remain on the high side of climo \naverages. \n\nBy the time the weekend ends, the front will shift off and Bertha \nwill be nothing more than a memory. Conditions will largely return \nto what we've been experiencing for most of the summer with a slight \nchance for afternoon thunderstorms and temperatures in the upper 80s \nand lower 90s. Heat risk concerns seem to creep into the forecast \nagain by this time next week, but a lot can change between now and \nthen.",
